WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.511
In enterprise AI, building a prototype is easy—

2
00:00:03.511 --> 00:00:08.353
surviving production cutover is where architectures stall.

3
00:00:08.353 --> 00:00:15.278
Migrating stateless workloads onto GPT-5.6, GPT-6, and GPT-6.1 exposes four coupled failure modes:

4
00:00:15.926 --> 00:00:19.227
silent prefix misses that trigger a 2.56× PTU spike,

5
00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:26.334
HTTP 429 gateway storms and buffered SSE stalls, cold-cache regional failover surges,

6
00:00:26.521 --> 00:00:29.683
and unsandboxed agent tools with flaky CI evals.

7
00:00:30.306 --> 00:00:36.193
Welcome to the Enterprise Azure AI Solution Industrialization Hub, version 2.0.

8
00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:39.324
Built for Cloud Solution Architects and platform teams,

9
00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:44.281
this governed workbench unites four live full-stack playbooks across 33 chapters,

10
00:00:44.281 --> 00:00:50.518
a regulated compliance profile, a 5-tool interactive Decision Studio, two printable white papers,

11
00:00:50.518 --> 00:00:53.632
five MIT release kits, and 52 cutover controls.

12
00:00:54.258 --> 00:00:58.427
Playbook 01 and its Regulated Multi-Engagement Profile govern

13
00:00:58.427 --> 00:01:02.468
context assembly and PTU economics across 15 chapters.

14
00:01:02.468 --> 00:01:08.573
Enforce the 6-position Scope-by-Volatility prefix stack, shard hot cache keys above 15 RPM,

15
00:01:08.573 --> 00:01:11.764
and size capacity with two-regime math—

16
00:01:11.764 --> 00:01:17.675
contrasting GPT-5.6 zero-weight cached reads against GPT-6 and 6.1 normalized read-write weights.

17
00:01:17.675 --> 00:01:21.364
Paired with Posture A ethical walls and workpaper lineage,

18
00:01:21.364 --> 00:01:25.376
you eliminate capacity spikes and save 71% on seasonal filing cliffs.

19
00:01:25.993 --> 00:01:32.650
Playbook 02 centralizes traffic behind a Multi-Backend Microsoft Foundry APIM AI Gateway.

20
00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:34.778
It enforces keyless Managed Identity RBAC,

21
00:01:34.778 --> 00:01:39.244
trips Retry-After circuit breakers from primary PTU-M to Standard PAYG,

22
00:01:39.244 --> 00:01:46.502
snapshots and restores request bodies around GPT-5.6 breakpoint stripping, streams unbuffered Server-Sent Events,

23
00:01:46.502 --> 00:01:51.606
and extracts out-of-band cost-center headers into OpenTelemetry FinOps metrics.

24
00:01:52.235 --> 00:01:55.930
Playbook 03 engineers continuity at the full AI Stamp level.

25
00:01:55.930 --> 00:02:02.216
It aligns Global, Data Zone, and Regional sovereignty across primary and disaster-recovery legs,

26
00:02:02.216 --> 00:02:08.952
sizes secondary PAYG buffers to absorb the 2.56× cold-cache failover surge without doubling idle PTUs,

27
00:02:08.952 --> 00:02:14.347
and synchronizes Cosmos DB state and dual Azure AI Search stamps for <15s Game-Day failover.

28
00:02:14.981 --> 00:02:20.523
Playbook 04 industrializes multi-step agents across a 3-tier sandboxed runtime.

29
00:02:20.831 --> 00:02:24.812
A stateless SDK-free orchestrator proxies typed AG-UI streams from one

30
00:02:24.812 --> 00:02:27.773
microVM container per session in Azure Container Apps Dynamic Sessions,

31
00:02:27.773 --> 00:02:32.214
converts binary documents into faithful Markdown via Content Understanding,

32
00:02:32.214 --> 00:02:36.110
retrieves ACL-trimmed citations through Foundry IQ MCP,

33
00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:40.413
and blocks regressions with 7-layer deterministic evaluations.

34
00:02:41.032 --> 00:02:43.758
In the browser-native Architecture Decision Studio,

35
00:02:43.758 --> 00:02:48.722
five client-side calculators model every design decision live with zero external telemetry:

36
00:02:48.722 --> 00:02:54.227
the two-regime PTU and spillover TCO simulator, the SKU-aware APIM XML policy builder,

37
00:02:54.377 --> 00:02:58.802
the multi-region cold-cache surge advisor, the ACA sandbox and contract builder,

38
00:02:59.013 --> 00:03:01.278
and the 30-minute 8-boundary intake triage.

39
00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:05.142
Every track ships drop-in deliverables rather than static slideware:

40
00:03:05.547 --> 00:03:10.305
two print-ready executive white papers, five zero-dependency MIT kits—

41
00:03:10.305 --> 00:03:15.227
including the PCR Python AST linter, agent trace and cross-region snapshot parity CLIs,

42
00:03:15.414 --> 00:03:19.140
APIM spillover XML, and two Application Insights KQL gates—

43
00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:23.661
plus 52 pull-request checklists and four companion open-source harnesses.

44
00:03:24.309 --> 00:03:30.259
Underneath sits a 5-stage industrialization factory with 4-tier Microsoft Learn evidence tagging,

45
00:03:30.259 --> 00:03:37.480
automated CI sanitization, pre-publication IP screening, and a repeatable 3-week customer delivery sprint.

46
00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:38.572
Even better,

47
00:03:38.572 --> 00:03:41.375
a built-in 24/7 dual-agent loop pairs an isolated improver agent

48
00:03:41.375 --> 00:03:45.587
with an independent ARB reviewer agent to continuously harden tests,

49
00:03:45.587 --> 00:03:47.026
kits, and live GitHub Pages.

50
00:03:47.649 --> 00:03:50.869
Put the full-stack Hub to work on your next Foundry architecture review:

51
00:03:51.262 --> 00:03:53.879
simulate sizing and policies in the Decision Studio,

52
00:03:54.066 --> 00:03:56.372
wire the five MIT gates and 52 checklists into CI,

53
00:03:56.372 --> 00:04:00.207
